{"packet_id":"D052-02","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit liability on transfer of the dwelling unit","requirement":"When a lessor transfers his interest in the dwelling unit, he stays liable under this section until the rental advance is credited to the successor and the tenant is notified in writing, or the advance plus accrued interest is credited to the tenant; if the lessor fails to credit the successor, the successor assumes liability.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units covered by G.L. c. 186, § 15B; liability attaches to the successor in interest without regard to the nature of the transfer.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"The liability does not apply to a city or town that acquires title to property under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a financial institution chartered by the commonwealth or the United States.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"In the event that the lessor fails to credit said rental advance to his successor in interest as required by this subsection, the successor in interest shall, without regard to the nature of the transfer, assume liability for crediting of the rental advance, and payment of all interest thereon to the tenant in accordance with the provisions of this section","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-02","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit law anti-waiver provision","requirement":"Any lease provision that conflicts with this section, and any waiver by a tenant or prospective tenant of any provision of this section, is against public policy and is void and unenforceable.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Leases and tenancies governed by G.L. c. 186, § 15B, and tenants or prospective tenants under them.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"Any provision of a lease which conflicts with any provision of this section and any waiver by a tenant or prospective tenant of any provision of this section shall be deemed to be against public policy and therefore void and unenforceable.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-02","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Short-term vacation rental exclusion from security deposit law","requirement":"The security deposit provisions of this section do not apply to any lease, rental, occupancy or tenancy of one hundred days or less that is for a vacation or recreational purpose.","key_value":"100 days or less","coverage_conditions":"All leases, rentals, occupancies and tenancies of 100 days or less in duration for vacation or recreational purposes are excluded from G.L. c. 186, § 15B.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Vacation or recreational rental of 100 days or less"},"exemptions":"Leases, rentals, occupancies or tenancies of one hundred days or less in duration for a vacation or recreational purpose.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"The provisions of this section shall not apply to any lease, rental, occupancy or tenancy of one hundred days or less in duration which lease or rental is for a vacation or recreational purpose.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
